WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.900
- On the flip side of how
you make a union work,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.563
I can't think of any one,

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.620
and Ruth Bader Ginsburg,

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:12.900
who I've just spent the last
week voraciously studying,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.510
and if you're watching her documentary,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.050
Gloria Steinem comes up,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.350
and Gloria Steinem is one
of the great world changers,

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.620
game changers, and when she
came up into your world,

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.520
how fast was it before you
said yes to portraying her?

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.800
- Oh man, it was immediate.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.707
Julie Taymor contacted me
about it and I was like,

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:36.120
"Yes, absolutely. I would
love to be a part of this."

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.020
I don't think it was after,
it wasn't until after that,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.300
that I really thought
about what it would entail.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.150
She's so iconic, and she's so
meaningful to so many people

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.670
and has been emblematic, I think,

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.357
of the women's movement
in the United States.

00:00:50.357 --> 00:00:54.320
So I also didn't realize
how challenging it would be

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.393
because she is,

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:00.900
she's actually has a quiet
recessive quality sometimes.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.610
She's known as one of the
world's great listeners.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.650
So it's not a very active
thing to play as an actor,

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.230
and her speech pattern is,

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:13.190
her inner accent is very
unique and, but she's not,

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.540
she's someone who will step back

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.083
and promote other people and
their activism and their words.

00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:25.083
And so it was very, very
challenging, but so fantastic.

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:29.580
Just trying to absorb
who she was in that way.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.750
- I think for as much as
I care about everyone,

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.630
and I'm such a people person,

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.650
I'm not sure I'm
comfortable in the silences.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.990
I definitely am a good listener,
but I'm a huge talker also.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.110
And these women,

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:46.550
they just possess sort
of an inner confidence,

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:50.170
which is so admirable,
but what they do with it

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:53.530
is all this outward protection of others.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.670
- Absolutely.

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.890
One of the things that
really struck me about Gloria

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.280
is that she's not
reactive. She's not rash.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.240
People said really horrific things to her.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.080
They just loaded it on her.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.850
And she always came from
a point of, like I said,

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.770
she would listen, she'd wait.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.330
And then she would respond,

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:15.360
but she never responded
with any kind of heat.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.500
She always responded with intellect,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.110
and she wasn't cruel to anyone ever

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.070
and incredibly tolerant
of other people's views.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.690
So I do think about that.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.657
I really think when I'm
talking to people, I'm like,

00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:30.007
"What would Gloria do?
How would she react?"

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.230
Maybe take take the time
to be more like her.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.280
- You're not going to
want to miss this movie.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.319
Julie Taymor does direct
and she's such a visionary.

00:02:40.319 --> 00:02:41.377
- Yeah, she really is.

00:02:41.377 --> 00:02:43.010
- And this film is no exception.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.820
I think the Glorias are dissected in ways

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.990
that are very unprecedented and unique.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:51.690
And there's an incredible
big surprise ending

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.000
that you won't want to miss,

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.459
and really quickly, "Dear Evan Hansen."

00:02:56.459 --> 00:02:57.292
(Julie laughing)

00:02:57.292 --> 00:02:58.553
(screams)
I love his play so much.

00:02:58.553 --> 00:03:00.158
- That's how I feel too.

00:03:00.158 --> 00:03:02.380
- Oh my god, are you excited?

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.120
- I am so excited. I'm beside myself.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.680
Honestly, I can't believe it.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:11.240
It's really, yeah. I
can't believe it happened.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:16.240
- This story I also feel is
just so important for people.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.480
We talk about mental health.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.520
We talk about all these issues now

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.100
that are trying to be
more in the forefront

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.040
and on the table.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.490
And then Ben Platt, a role
he seemed born to play.

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.470
And for a lot of people watching the play

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.900
was the moment everything really clicks

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.600
as his relationship with his mother,

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:38.790
and you'll be playing her,
and I'm so excited for this

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:42.220
to have everyone have access to it.

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.420
- Oh, I feel so lucky

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.050
and it really is a
beautiful, beautiful piece.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.220
And I think it will
make a wonderful movie.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.240
- I think so too.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.460
And I have just the biggest
pompoms rooting you on always.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.370
And thank you so much

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.427
for gracing our show with your presence.

00:03:58.427 --> 00:04:02.133
"The Glorias" will be available
streaming on Amazon Prime.

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:04.716
(upbeat music)

